cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If CIRCLE informs your research, please cite it as below."
title: "CIRCLE: an open-source resonance workbench for traceable physiological feedback"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Christopher
    family-names: Woodyard
    affiliation: Vers3Dynamics
repository-code: "https://github.com/topherchris420/circle"
url: "https://topherchris420.github.io/circle/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  CIRCLE is a simulation-based research workbench. It turns simulated
  physiological signals (PPG, EDA, IMU) into quality-gated decisions,
  bounded adaptive audio and visual feedback, and exported evidence that can
  be independently replayed and audited. It includes a consent gate, active
  and sham session controls, an offline browser demo, acquisition adapters,
  and Rev B hardware designs under engineering review. It is not a medical
  device and makes no physiological or therapeutic claim.
keywords:
  - physiology
  - biofeedback
  - closed-loop control
  - reproducibility
  - consent
  - simulation
  - neurotechnology
